  "body": "Write the user documentation guide for in-app AI chat and external MCP agent workflows.\n\n## Scope\n- Create `site/content/guide/ai.md`, link it in `site/content/guide/_index.md`, and update `site/content/guide/mcp.md`.\n- Document setup steps for every provider and external agent in `#1773`:\n  - In-app panel: Anthropic (Claude), OpenAI (GPT/Codex), Google Gemini, Ollama (`http://localhost:11434`), Unsloth Studio (`http://127.0.0.1:8888`), LM Studio (`http://localhost:1234/v1`), `llama-server` (`--jinja`), and offline-only mode.\n  - External agents (`--mcp-port` plus `camcraft-cli mcp --connect`): Claude Code, Codex CLI, Gemini and Antigravity CLI, and headless `camcraft-cli mcp` scripting.\n- Write complete worked CAM examples for four tasks:\n  1. Import a model and create a setup and stock.\n  2. Add a 2D Pocket on a picked face, generate toolpaths, and read warnings.\n  3. Change a parameter and undo the turn.\n  4. Verify a program and post G-code with panel confirmation.\n- Explain safety, privacy, API key storage, and troubleshooting (models without tool calling, small context windows, connection refused, and rejected keys).\n- Check every command flag and MCP tool name in the guide against live `tools::list()` in automated tests.\n\nDone means: The `site/content/guide/ai.md` guide builds cleanly in the `site/` pipeline, covers every provider, external agent, and all four CAM tasks, and passes tool-name verification against `tools::list()`.\n\nPart of #1773\n",
